-- title:
--   Diamond ⟨ e⟩⁻¹ on the j-finite chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M$ with $M\neq 0$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, a divisibility $p\mid M$ with $M/p\neq 0$, a proof `hj` that the Laurent series $\mathtt{jqModC}\,\mathbb Q=q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral }j\text{-numerator power series})$ lies in $\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb Q\,\top$, the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the integral form ratios at full level, and a unit $e\in(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$. Write $F$ for $\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb Q\,(\mathtt{\Gamma N}\,p\,M\,H\,hpM)$ and $A=\mathtt{chartAlgFin}$ for the $j$-finite chart algebra of the two-chart integral model, i.e. the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the subalgebra of the base ring `R p` generated by the element $\mathtt{jAt}$ determined by `hj`. The assertion is that there exists an `R p`-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $A$ such that for every $b\in A$ the coefficientwise embedding $\mathtt{coeffEmb}$ into $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ of the Laurent series underlying $\sigma b$ equals the Laurent series underlying the image of $\mathtt{coeffEmb}\,b$ — viewed, via base change of $b$'s membership, as an element of $\mathtt{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(M/p)\,(\mathtt{infSubgroup}\,p\,M\,H\,hpM)$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the level-$(M/p)$ function field for the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ — under the inverse of $\mathtt{diamondAutHBar}\,(M/p)\,(\mathtt{infSubgroup}\,p\,M\,H\,hpM)\,e$. Thus $\sigma$ reads as $\langle e\rangle^{-1}$ on $q$-expansions.
--
--   This is the statement that the diamond operator $\langle e\rangle$ at level $M/p$ preserves the integral closure of $\mathrm{R}_p[j]$ in the level-$(M/p)$ modular function field, so that it acts by an `R p`-algebra automorphism of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model; classically this is part of the description of diamond operators on integral models of modular curves. It is used in the chart-level description of the diamond action on the Deligne–Rapoport model at $p$, via [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_placeOfPoint_fibreMap_dia0_eq_diamondActionModL_smul_of_ker_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_placeOfPoint_fibreMap_dia0_eq_diamondActionModL_smul_of_ker_le).
